<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<TestCaseEntity>
   <description>Mirrors Jira PT-268 (manually tested/passed 6/17/2026 by Lejla): when show-react-portal-poc is ON for a supplier with active FusionAuth registrations, the React shell renders with the SCiSupplier iframe experience instead of falling back. Uses ffOnSupplierEmail (Regression profile), an account confirmed flagged-in as of 6/17/2026 — reconfirm current flag state with Lejla/PostHog before trusting a failure as a real regression vs. a stale flag assumption. Login selectors verified live 9/21/2026; requires VPN/Tailscale to reach regression.primerevenue.com. Updated 10/1/2026 now that the 2FA blocker is resolved: login actually reaches a &quot;Switch Company&quot; account-switcher step (inside an iframe) that every prior run was blocked from seeing. This account has multiple companies — the test now loops through all of them via the `Data Files/SupplierCompanies` data file, confirming the shell renders for each one, then returns to the switcher between companies via the in-app &quot;Switch Company&quot; link (hover the current-company header dropdown, click the link). SCiSupplier content (&quot;Recent Activity&quot;) lives inside the shell iframe, so it is checked via the captured `div_Recent Activity` object (its ref_element makes Katalon switch frames) rather than a page-text search, which only sees the outer document. First full pass across all 3 companies 10/1/2026.</description>
   <name>TC_FeatureFlag_ShellRendersWhenOn</name>
   <tag></tag>
   <comment></comment>
   <recordOption>OTHER</recordOption>
